rdmaproxy: accept mlx5 data-direct uverbs calls

Backport of upstream gVisor commit 574094148cae18e739634382c0a28d60520c319a
("Accept mlx5 data-direct uverbs calls in rdmaproxy",
https://github.com/google/gvisor/pull/17524, merged 2026-11-21), which no
release has yet (the newest is release-20261116.0). Its diff is unchanged;
drop this patch when moving to a release that has it.

What: rdmaproxy, gVisor's proxy of the host's /dev/infiniband/uverbs*
devices (--rdmaproxy), passes two mlx5 "data direct" calls to the host
instead of failing them with EINVAL: the method
MLX5_IB_METHOD_GET_DATA_DIRECT_SYSFS_PATH (0x1001) of the device object,
whose one attribute is a buffer the host kernel fills with a sysfs path, and
the attribute MLX5_IB_ATTR_REG_DMABUF_MR_ACCESS_FLAGS (0x1000) of
UVERBS_METHOD_REG_DMABUF_MR, an inline u32 of flags. The attribute goes into
the core schema, so other drivers' devices accept it too; the host driver
validates it.

Why: the libmlx5 of a newer rdma-core, such as the AWS EFA installer 1.47's,
makes both calls. NCCL's NET/IB transport then failed to initialize on
Mellanox HCAs under gVisor and NCCL fell back to TCP sockets without an
error; the Sentry logged "rdmaproxy: unsupported ioctl object=0
method=4097" and "rdmaproxy: unsupported attr id=0x1000 on object=7
method=4". The libmlx5 of Ubuntu's rdma-core makes neither call.

Verified: upstream built //pkg/sentry/devices/rdmaproxy/... and
//pkg/abi/ib and, on an mlx5 host with an EFA-installer image, NCCL selected
NET/IB and moved its traffic over RDMA. Here, the diff applies unchanged
after 0001 to 0010 to the same three files as the pull request's base, and
runsc builds with it.

diff --git a/pkg/abi/ib/ib.go b/pkg/abi/ib/ib.go
index ba1053ee646..06aa4163917 100644
--- a/pkg/abi/ib/ib.go
+++ b/pkg/abi/ib/ib.go
@@ -301,6 +301,15 @@ const (
 const (
 	MLX5_IB_OBJECT_UAR = 0x1008
 
+	// enum mlx5_ib_device_methods.
+	MLX5_IB_METHOD_GET_DATA_DIRECT_SYSFS_PATH = 0x1001
+
+	// enum mlx5_ib_get_data_direct_sysfs_path_attrs.
+	MLX5_IB_ATTR_GET_DATA_DIRECT_SYSFS_PATH = 0x1000
+
+	// enum mlx5_ib_reg_dmabuf_mr_attrs.
+	MLX5_IB_ATTR_REG_DMABUF_MR_ACCESS_FLAGS = 0x1000
+
 	// enum mlx5_ib_uar_obj_methods.
 	MLX5_IB_METHOD_UAR_OBJ_ALLOC   = 0x1000
 	MLX5_IB_METHOD_UAR_OBJ_DESTROY = 0x1001
diff --git a/pkg/sentry/devices/rdmaproxy/cxproxy/cxproxy.go b/pkg/sentry/devices/rdmaproxy/cxproxy/cxproxy.go
index 094cea0f7f0..f70efd44d91 100644
